# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TIA Portal repository policy
#
# COMMIT:  the archive produced by  Project > Archive  (*.zap16, *.zap17, ...)
#          It is one self-contained file and it is what another engineer needs
#          in order to run  Project > Retrieve  and get a working project.
#
# NEVER COMMIT: the live project folder (*.ap16 / *.ap17 / ... and everything
#          under it). It is a binary working directory with lock files,
#          per-machine caches, compile output and a search index. It changes
#          on every open, it does not merge, and it is several hundred MB.
#
# If a .zap ever exceeds 100 MB, GitHub will reject the push. Use Git LFS:
#     git lfs install
#     git lfs track "*.zap16"
#     git add .gitattributes
#     git add labs/<lab>/src/<project>.zap16
#     git commit -m "Add archived TIA project via LFS"
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Live TIA Portal project directories -- never commit these
*.ap1[0-9]/
*.ap[0-9][0-9]/
*.ap1[0-9]
*.ap[0-9][0-9]
*.al[0-9][0-9]

# TIA working directories, wherever they appear
Logs/
TMP/
System/
Vci/
XRef/
IM/
AdditionalFiles/
UserFiles/
**/SearchIndex/
**/PEData/
*.plf
*.idx
*.db
~$*
~PEData.*

# TIA / WinCC scratch
*.bak
*.tmp
*.temp
*.s7pbak
*.wbak

# Simulation
*.sim1[0-9]
Simulation/

# Keep the archives -- they are the deliverable
!*.zap1[0-9]
!*.zap[0-9][0-9]

# Editors and IDEs
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
